# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# This is not .dockerignore. That one filters the build context *after* the
# upload, so anything listed only there is still paid for in upload time on
# every deploy. Before this file existed a submit was 4.1 GiB and 192,089
# files, most of which Docker then discarded.
#
# Creating this file also disables gcloud's auto-generation from .gitignore,
# which is why the include directive below is mandatory rather than tidy.

.git
.gitignore

#!include:.gitignore

# Other Claude sessions' git worktrees. Each carries its own node_modules and
# build output. 3.4 GiB at the time of writing, and .dockerignore drops the
# whole .claude tree from the image regardless. The tracked part of .claude
# (skills, launch.json) is not needed to build either, but is small and stays
# so that this file has one job.
.claude/worktrees/

# Angular's local build cache. Regenerated in the image.
.angular/

# Nested workspaces. `#!include:.gitignore` pulls in the ROOT .gitignore only,
# and its `/node_modules` is root-anchored, so `web/node_modules` (299 MiB) and
# `functions/node_modules` (237 MiB) were uploading on every build. They are
# ignored locally by web/.gitignore and functions/.gitignore, which gcloud never
# reads. Unanchored, so any depth is covered.
node_modules/
dist/
.angular/
